      "problem": "Let $V={R}_{1}[t],$ the vector space of real polynomials of degree at most $1,$ and let the inner product on $V$ be defined as\n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1).\n$$\n\nNow consider the following elements of $V:$\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=5t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=-2t+2,\\,q(t)=-t-4\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $S=\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\}$ given that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the inner product, and that the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1}(t)\\}$ equals $-5t.$",
